+# v41 — Safe gem collection and faster Gem Sniper sweep
+
+Confirmed gems beside the floating portrait, under chat or near an edge now
+trigger a gameplay camera drag in clear central ground. Loong Lens measures
+terrain movement, re-detects the same gem and clicks its fresh position only
+when the whole gem is clear of the interface. It can correct the camera response
+and try up to three drags. If it cannot confirm movement or reacquire the target,
+it pauses without tapping the HUD. F10 releases input and stays stopped.
+Safe gems retain their existing direct click. Each encounter retains one original
+photo and one history/counter entry. Gem Spy remains observation-only.
+
+**Fast map sweep**, enabled by default in Sniper settings, starts inspection after
+two rendered, stable gameplay observations instead of always waiting the default
+0.5 seconds. Blank or changing scenes keep the loading wait. Custom loading waits
+stay fixed. A late scene change restarts the full inspection window and clears
+old detection evidence. The existing three-hit/0.8-second confirmation, inspection
+duration, 20-second collection wait and Emerald Corner return remain unchanged.
+Turn Fast map sweep off to restore fixed loading waits. Spy timing is unchanged.
+
+This update keeps v40's compact UI, MuMuPlayer 6.8.9 Windows mouse input, routes,
+map assets, detector, histories, daily Obtained choices and Endless mode. Keep
+MuMu visible, uncovered and focused; no ADB is used. Settings/history stay in
+LocalAppData. Exit the old app, extract the whole new folder and run LoongLens.exe.
+
+Validation covers translated gameplay fixtures, portrait/chat/edge collection,
+camera response and cancellation, native Windows capture/drag/click/hotkeys in a
+procedural game window, source/frozen app checks and a full-route comparison.
+The comparison uses already-rendered simulated gameplay; live MuMu performance
+and actual game camera behavior cannot be measured in the build environment.
